      ],
      "explanation": "Because the requested product contains \\(d-1\\) and \\(e-1\\), it is useful to check whether \\(1\\) is a solution of the equation. Substituting \\(x=1\\) gives\n\\[\n2(1)^2+3(1)-5=2+3-5=0.\n\\]\nThus one of the two solutions \\(d\\) and \\(e\\) equals \\(1\\). The corresponding factor in \\((d-1)(e-1)\\) is zero, so the product is \\(\\boxed{0}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
